date-released: 2026-09-28
keywords:
  - brane-world cosmology
  - extra dimensions
  - Big Bang
  - five-dimensional gravity
  - Einstein–scalar gravity
  - numerical relativity
  - de Sitter brane
  - junction conditions
abstract: >-
  HDBLAST is a speculative, testable research hypothesis asking whether a gravitational event in
  a fifth dimension could have transferred energy into our four-dimensional universe and started
  the hot Big Bang. The program registers a specific five-dimensional Einstein–scalar shell
  model and publishes certified, exact and numerical results, together with negative results
  and corrections. The September 2026 checkpoints correct the static late-time branch and
  propose a matter extension. No hot Big Bang mechanism or observational signal is claimed.
